# GitHub Setup Guide

## Suggested Repository Name
`arduino-smart-fire-detection-suppression`

## Short Description (About box)
Educational Arduino fire-detection prototype with flame and MQ-2 sensing, filtering, latched alarm, buzzer/LED warnings, and a simulated suppression output. Not a certified fire alarm.

## Topics
`arduino` `arduino-uno` `fire-detection` `fire-alarm` `flame-sensor` `mq2` `embedded-systems` `iot` `electronics` `student-project` `state-machine` `safety-systems`

## Upload Steps
1. Create a new empty repository on GitHub (no README, since this ZIP already contains one).
2. Extract the ZIP on your computer.
3. In the extracted folder run:
```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: educational Arduino fire detection prototype"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/arduino-smart-fire-detection-suppression.git
git push -u origin main
```
Or use the GitHub web UI: **Add file → Upload files** and drag the extracted contents.

## Photographs to Capture (only real photos of your build)
1. Full circuit from above with all components visible.
2. Close-up of Arduino wiring.
3. Close-up of flame sensor and MQ-2 mounting.
4. Normal state (green LED on).
5. Pre-alarm state (red blinking).
6. Alarm state with simulated suppression LED on.
7. Serial Monitor screenshot with diagnostics.
8. Fault state demonstration.
9. Hand-drawn or digital wiring diagram next to the real circuit.

Save images in an `images/` folder and reference them from the README.
